INT. COASTAL RADAR SHACK - NIGHT, 1944

Plywood walls. A glowing scope. A kettle on a hot plate. Rain on tin.

CORPORAL AGNES TILLMAN-REED, 20s, headset, hunches at the scope. SERGEANT BARTHOLOMEW OYELOWO, 40s, reads a magazine upside down. PRIVATE LUCIEN FAIVRE, 19, stirs tea he isn't drinking.

She taps the glass. Leans closer.

AGNES
Contact. Bearing two-seven-zero.

He drops the magazine. Rolls the chair beside her.

BART
Range?

AGNES
Thirty miles. Slow.

BART
Ours?

AGNES
No transponder.

He swears under his breath. The other boy stops stirring.

LUCIEN
Should I wake the captain?

BART
Not yet. Let it come.

The radio crackles on the shelf.

COMMANDER HALLORAN (V.O.)
(through static)
Shack Seven, Halloran. Report.

Bart grabs the handset. Agnes turns the dial.

BART
Single contact. Unidentified. Approaching.

HALLORAN (V.O.)
Hold position. Do not engage.

BART
Understood, sir.

He sets the handset down. She watches the scope. The blip crawls.

AGNES
Closing.

LUCIEN
Maybe it's a fishing boat.

BART
At night, in a blackout?

He doesn't answer. He pours the tea down the sink.

The blip stops. Hangs. Starts to fade.

AGNES
It's turning.

She leans back. Exhales. He rubs his face with both hands.

BART
Good.

The radio crackles again.

HALLORAN (V.O.)
Shack Seven, stand down. It was ours.

Bart picks up the magazine. Right side up this time.
